WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.403
-Our next guest is a comedian
and actor you know from

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:04.603
his work on shows such as
"The Middle,"

00:00:04.603 --> 00:00:05.705
"Saturday Night Live,"

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.440
and movies like
"A Night at the Roxbury."

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.475
He stars in "Famous,"
which is in theaters

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:11.277
and available on demand
December 10th.

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:13.112
Please welcome to the show
our very good friend

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:14.614
Chris Kattan, everybody.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.649
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.642
Christopher!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:43.642 --> 00:00:45.311
How are you, buddy?
-I'm great. How are you?

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:47.346
-It's so great to have you
not just in New York,

00:00:47.346 --> 00:00:48.915
but back in the building
where we met.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:50.917
You flew from L.A. yesterday?

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:52.051
-I did.
-How was your flight? Good?

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:53.319
-Oh, thank you for asking.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.688
-Good. That was the thing
about our friendship.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.924
We always checked in about how
each other's flights went.

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:59.392
-Yeah, I did that last week.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.727
I said, "How was your flight?",
and you weren't even on one.

00:01:01.727 --> 00:01:03.430
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.331
-But I like the care that you
took to just check to make sure.

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:09.502
-I'm very caring about you
and your flights.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:10.670
-Always, from the day we met.
-Always.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.037
-How's the miles, the mileage?

00:01:12.037 --> 00:01:13.673
-Oh, my miles -- it's a little
down because of COVID.

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:15.874
-Ooh! Ooh, yeah.

00:01:15.874 --> 00:01:18.978
-I've lost a bit of my status
on some of the majors.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.346
-I also got your message about

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:23.883
you asking me about my miles,
and I never answered.

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.818
-Okay. How are your miles?

00:01:25.818 --> 00:01:27.587
-Not so good, as well.
-Okay.

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:28.621
How was your flight yesterday?

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:32.926
-It was good.
Thanks again for asking.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.193
It was good.

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:38.597
I sat next to, interestingly
enough, Helen Hunt,

00:01:38.597 --> 00:01:41.801
but I didn't know it was her,
because we have masks on.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.536
So we had no idea.

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:46.005
She had no idea it was me,
and I had no idea it was her.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:49.309
But I met her years ago,
'cause she was friends with

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:52.312
my dad, and my dad was one of
the founders of The Groundlings.

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:54.113
You know The Groundlings.
-Yeah, of course.

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:56.949
So did you figure out on the way
off the plane that you were?

00:01:56.949 --> 00:01:59.685
-It was 10 minutes before,
and I was kind of like,

00:01:59.685 --> 00:02:01.453
"Why didn't you say anything?"

00:02:01.453 --> 00:02:03.489
And she was also like,
"Why didn't you say anything?"

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:05.258
-Yeah.
-And we got into a little tiff.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.193
-Oh. So it ended badly?

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:09.762
-No, there was a minute before
I got off the plane

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.264
that it ended up being okay.

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.365
Because I said,
"The last time I saw you,

00:02:13.365 --> 00:02:15.635
you were hosting 'SNL.'"

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:17.603
And she hosted
'cause she was pushing, I think,

00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:18.638
"As Good as It Gets"
at that time.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:19.672
-Yeah.

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.808
-And Hanson was
the musical guest.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.042
I don't know if
you remember Hanson.

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:24.644
[ Cheers and applause ]
Well, don't get --

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:26.378
They're not here, so...

00:02:26.378 --> 00:02:27.914
Maybe one member is.

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:29.281
Why would --
They're like, "Yay!"

00:02:29.281 --> 00:02:31.450
Anyway...
But Hanson was the guest.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:35.688
-You gestured to them.
You elicited that response.

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:37.357
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Well...

00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:40.660
-That's not for you!

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.362
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.362 --> 00:02:44.897
-I got so excited.

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:46.999
Every time somebody
says "Hanson," I get excited.

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:49.402
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:54.940
-But, so, anyway,
one of the Hanson brothers?

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.075
-Yeah.
-Thank you.

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:59.945
And -- Was running
up and down the hallway,

00:02:59.945 --> 00:03:02.782
and she said,
"Stop running, Hanson!",

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.784
'cause she didn't know
the name of that Hanson.

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:06.051
-Yeah. You know what's
interesting about seeing

00:03:06.051 --> 00:03:07.053
Helen Hunt on an airplane?

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:08.321
-Yes.

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:10.323
-Maybe one of the stars of
one of the most famous

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:12.091
"SNL" airplane sketches
of all time.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:13.326
-Is?
-"Buh-bye."

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:15.194
-Oh, right, "Buh-bye."
Yes, with David Spade.

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:16.495
Very good.
-Maybe you'll see it later.

00:03:16.495 --> 00:03:18.764
Not as popular as Hanson,
but it has some --

00:03:18.764 --> 00:03:20.799
-You'd think the meter is,
you know...

00:03:20.799 --> 00:03:23.001
-I owe you a lot.
I owe you my world.

00:03:23.001 --> 00:03:24.103
-Oh, no, yes, your world.

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.471
-Yeah. I mean this with
all sincerity.

00:03:26.471 --> 00:03:27.573
You know this, obviously.

00:03:27.573 --> 00:03:29.208
I think some people
might know this.

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:31.944
I met my wife at your wedding.

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:33.779
-Yes, you did.

00:03:33.779 --> 00:03:36.115
-And now we got
three kids, and --

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:37.449
-And it's all 'cause of me!

00:03:37.449 --> 00:03:39.185
-It's all thanks to you
inviting me to your wedding.

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:41.821
I did not know my wife,
and I met her there.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:47.393
-Right. And I like that you
tell that story to people.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:49.261
However,
I'm not married anymore.

00:03:49.261 --> 00:03:50.630
-No.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:58.004
-So if you can not put a period
after the wedding part

00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:01.107
and just say -- and conclude,

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:05.978
"I met my wife at Chris Kattan's
wedding, however..."

00:04:05.978 --> 00:04:08.080
-Oh. You want me to make sure
that's in there, as well.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.382
-That I'm not married anymore.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:04:10.382 --> 00:04:11.383
-Well, just 'cause that's true.

00:04:11.383 --> 00:04:12.552
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:14.087
-I can make sure
I get that in there, as well.

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:15.488
-If you don't mind.
-Yeah.

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:19.058
-But we have communication
about airplanes,

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.392
so I'll probably
get that message.

00:04:20.392 --> 00:04:22.527
-I feel like we're
the legacy of your wedding now.

00:04:22.527 --> 00:04:24.096
We have to -- you know...

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:25.798
-You are.
-Yeah.

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:28.434
-Can I say your wife's name?
-No, you can't. I'm sorry.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.203
-I'm gonna get in trouble?

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:32.872
-We've been together for
13 years,

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:33.940
but we are keeping her
name under wraps.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.876
-Her name quiet.
Yeah, I saw that.

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:38.778
I went on Instagram like,
"Wait a second.

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:39.879
It's blocked."

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:41.214
-If you just don't mind saying

00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:43.849
"Seth Meyers' wife --
lady -- wife lady."

00:04:43.849 --> 00:04:45.417
-Wife lady.
-Yeah.

00:04:45.417 --> 00:04:46.952
-That's weird.

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:49.855
Remember the good old days,
when we used to say "lady wife"?

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:51.657
-Yeah. Can't say that anymore.

00:04:51.657 --> 00:04:52.758
-Not anymore.

00:04:52.758 --> 00:04:53.892
-Yeah, Alexi.

00:04:53.892 --> 00:04:55.728
-Yes, Alexi, lovely lady.

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:59.098
You met at my wedding,
which didn't go too far.

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:00.465
-You know what?
It didn't go too far.

00:05:00.465 --> 00:05:02.668
-But that's okay.
-No, it's fine.

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:03.936
Yeah, of course.
-Yeah.

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:05.771
-But I do want to point out,
'cause now that

00:05:05.771 --> 00:05:07.407
you've opened the doors that
I'm allowed to say

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:09.375
that you're not married anymore,

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:12.311
we went out for our
year anniversary of dating,

00:05:12.311 --> 00:05:16.048
Alexi and I,
and you were already divorced.

00:05:16.048 --> 00:05:17.717
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:22.121
-And I say that
because you were --

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:24.389
-Well, you say that
'cause that was true.

00:05:24.389 --> 00:05:27.092
-That was true, but, also,
you were at the restaurant

00:05:27.092 --> 00:05:28.094
with a different person.

00:05:28.094 --> 00:05:29.695
-With a person.
-Yeah.

00:05:29.695 --> 00:05:30.963
-That's how you found out.

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:33.699
-And you walked over to
the table and you said,

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:34.967
"What are you guys doing?"

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:38.738
And Alexi said,
"It's our one-year anniversary,

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:41.540
and you went like this,
"Oh, right!"

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.409
-Is that how I sound?

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:45.077
-No, that night,
you sounded like that.

00:05:45.077 --> 00:05:47.780
-If that's how I sound
when you tell that story

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.815
about meeting your wife
at my wedding --

00:05:49.815 --> 00:05:51.984
"Chris said, 'Oh, right!'" --

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:53.386
then please don't
ever acknowledge

00:05:53.386 --> 00:05:54.754
that you met your wife
at my wedding.

00:05:54.754 --> 00:05:56.555
-Okay, you came over,
and were like, "How wonderful."

00:05:56.555 --> 00:05:58.958
-Thank you. That's much better.
That I like.

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:01.794
-You were telling me backstage
your mom was very concerned.

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:03.028
She didn't know
we have that great bit

00:06:03.028 --> 00:06:04.897
about how we talk about
airline miles.

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:06.999
She was helping you
come up with bits,

00:06:06.999 --> 00:06:08.333
things to talk about
on the talk show.

00:06:08.333 --> 00:06:10.837
-Right, 'cause I was coming on
the show, which I am now.

00:06:10.837 --> 00:06:11.904
-Yeah.

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:13.305
-And --
[ Light laughter ]

00:06:13.305 --> 00:06:17.175
Thanks. And I was like,
"Mom, I don't know what to say.

00:06:17.175 --> 00:06:18.510
I'm a little nervous.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:21.514
You know, I don't know
what kind of stories to tell."

00:06:21.514 --> 00:06:22.782
And she looked up online
and said,

00:06:22.782 --> 00:06:24.716
"Well, here's something
interesting.

00:06:24.716 --> 00:06:27.687
Viagra cures Alzheimer's."

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:29.088
-Hmm.

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:32.058
-And I said, "Mom, I don't think
that's an appropriate story

00:06:32.058 --> 00:06:34.126
to bring up or acknowledge,

00:06:34.126 --> 00:06:36.996
but I think the fact that
you said that is what's funny."

00:06:36.996 --> 00:06:38.464
-Yeah.
-That's a funny story.

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:39.965
-Yeah, right.
-That she brought that up.

00:06:39.965 --> 00:06:41.100
-So there you go.
She gave you --

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.134
-But!

00:06:42.134 --> 00:06:44.270
[ Laughs ]

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:45.438
Yeah.
-Do you have more on it?

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:47.273
Do you have, like,
the underlying science?

00:06:47.273 --> 00:06:48.741
-No.
-She didn't give you any?

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:50.109
Also, I like that she said,

00:06:50.109 --> 00:06:51.343
"Here's a good story," and then
she just gave you a fact.

00:06:51.343 --> 00:06:52.811
-I know. And then that was it.

00:06:52.811 --> 00:06:54.146
-Yeah.
-Yeah. Not really.

00:06:54.146 --> 00:06:55.881
Do you have any --
So, nothing else to share?

00:06:55.881 --> 00:06:59.084
-Oh, yes, I do have
a big announcement.

00:06:59.084 --> 00:07:01.286
-Okay.
Bigger than Viagra-Alzheimer's?

00:07:01.286 --> 00:07:03.890
-Oh, this is very -- What?

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:05.257
Anyway...

00:07:05.257 --> 00:07:10.129
But, yes, that Kim Kardashian
and Pete Davidson and I

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:11.797
are now going out.

00:07:11.797 --> 00:07:13.566
-Whoa!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:17.803 --> 00:07:19.605
This is big.
-It's a big deal.

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:20.806
-You got back in the game.

00:07:20.806 --> 00:07:23.809
-Yeah, I got back in the game
in a big way.

00:07:23.809 --> 00:07:25.244
But we may break up tomorrow.
-Oh, okay.

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:26.679
-We don't know
what's gonna happen.

00:07:26.679 --> 00:07:28.214
-We'll just check in as we go?
-Yeah, we'll just check in.

00:07:28.214 --> 00:07:29.248
-Alright, great.

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:30.516
I want to talk more
about the movie.

00:07:30.516 --> 00:07:31.884
We're gonna be right back
with Chris Kattan.

